## Running a backtest

### CLI

```bash
# Activate venv first
source .venv/bin/activate

# Default: research on the first RESEARCH_FRAC (50%) of days; score the unseen rest
python run_backtest.py

# Widen/narrow the research period — eval window is still "the rest"
python run_backtest.py --research-frac 0.4

# Explicit sub-window: score [500, 750), deliberately leaving [750, nt) untouched
# (the framework doesn't enforce that seal — it's on you)
python run_backtest.py --eval-start 500 --eval-end 750

# Truncate to first 1000 days, then score an explicit window within them
python run_backtest.py --max-days 1000 --eval-start 500 --eval-end 1000

# Match the official eval.py window exactly (days 751–1000)
python run_backtest.py --eval-start 751 --eval-end 1001

# Save all plots to a PDF
python run_backtest.py --plots report.pdf

# Walk-forward cross-validation (rolling out-of-sample windows)
python run_backtest.py --walk-forward --test-size 125

# Bootstrap confidence interval on score
python run_backtest.py --bootstrap --n-bootstrap 2000

# Full run — walk-forward + bootstrap + plots + all stats, auto-saved to results/<dataset>/<timestamp>/
python run_backtest.py --full
```

